9.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: 10 essential controls.

For a 5-color streptavidin-bead sort on AF350, GFP, PE, AF647 and AF750 the minimal set that will let you set correct voltages, perform accurate compensation and set sort gates reliably is:

* 1 unstained streptavidin bead control for bead autofluorescence and baseline autofluorescence;
* 5 single-stain compensation controls, one bead population stained with each fluorochrome individually: AF350, GFP, PE, AF647 and AF750;
* 4 FMO controls. FMOs are required to define the spillover-defined boundary for each marker in the presence of the other four. In practice the FMO for the last acquired channel, AF750, is functionally equivalent to the unstained bead control once compensation is applied, so the unstained control serves as the effective FMO for AF750.

That is 1 + 5 + 4 = 10 controls that are strictly required to get clean compensation matrices and sort gates for the five-channel panel. Extra controls such as a biotin-blocked bead or full minus-one replicates are useful for troubleshooting but are not essential for routine sorting.

